 "post": {
  "title": "You Said No to the Invite. They Barely Minded. #shorts",
  "description": "Ever said yes just to dodge the guilt? Send this to the friend who can't say no. Mae turned down Otto's barbecue and spent the night sure he was angry. In 'Saying no: The negative ramifications from invitation declines are less severe than we think' (Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, published online 2023), Julian Givi and Colleen Kirk ran five experiments with more than 2,000 people. People who declined an invitation expected the inviter to be angrier and more disappointed, and less likely to invite them again, than inviters actually were. In their pilot, 77% said they had accepted an invitation to something they didn't want to go to. A kind no costs less than you think. #psychology #shorts #peoplepleaser #overthinking #boundaries",
